sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant W2 as Worker 2
    participant Ctrl as Controller (Liveness & Repair)
    participant DB as SQLite Metadata
    participant W1 as Surviving Worker 1
    participant W3 as Target Worker 3
    participant C as Client

    Note over W1,W2: Normal state: Chunk c0 valid on [worker1, worker2] (healthy)
    W2--xCtrl: Worker 2 stops (heartbeats cease)
    Note over Ctrl,DB: Heartbeat age > HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUT (15s)
    Ctrl->>DB: worker2 status: ALIVE -> DEAD (dead_since=t0)
    Note over DB: Replica rows kept intact; chunk is under_replicated (valid=1)

    C->>Ctrl: GET /api/v1/objects/{id}
    Ctrl->>W1: GET /internal/chunks/c0 (fallback/skip DEAD worker2)
    W1-->>Ctrl: Verified bytes + SHA-256 match
    Ctrl-->>C: 200 OK (uninterrupted read continuity)

    Note over Ctrl: Inside REPAIR_GRACE_PERIOD (< 30s): Repair skipped (tolerates brief flaps)
    Note over Ctrl: Past REPAIR_GRACE_PERIOD (now - dead_since >= 30s): Repair eligible
    Ctrl->>W1: GET /internal/chunks/c0 + verify SHA-256 == DB checksum
    Ctrl->>W3: PUT /internal/chunks/c0 (X-Chunk-Checksum)
    W3-->>Ctrl: 201 Created
    Ctrl->>DB: INSERT replica (c0, worker3, OK) -> 2 valid replicas [W1, W3]

    W2->>Ctrl: Worker 2 restarts -> POST /internal/workers/register
    Ctrl->>DB: worker2 status: DEAD -> ALIVE (dead_since=NULL)
    Ctrl-->>W2: 200 OK immediately; schedule async reconcile_worker(worker2)
    Ctrl->>W2: GET /internal/workers/worker2/chunks
    Note over Ctrl: Chunk c0 now over-replicated (valid=3: W1, W2, W3)
    Ctrl->>W2: DELETE excess replica on highest-loaded worker
    Ctrl->>DB: DELETE excess replica row -> back to R=2
